<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thurisind</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 560</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thurisind was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a> from about 548 to about 560. His reign was dominated by war with the neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> under Audoin, in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> supported each side in turn; his son Turismod was killed by Audoin's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alboin">Alboin</a> in battle around 551. He was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunimund">Cunimund</a>, the last Gepid king.</p></div>
